      "writtenOn": "2025-10-25T09:46:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this makes sense in the current code, however if anyone wants to add an additional flag like `FT_LOAD_VERTICAL_LAYOUT` or `FT_LOAD_NO_BITMAP` in the future, then it would be more difficult to use this method to apply these flags (It might require the function to be changed back to `FT_Int32 args`).\n\nRight now, I feel it wouldn\u0027t really save more than a line or so, because even though all the the callers may have 3-4 lines less at the end, the function itself would be about 2-3 lines longer.\n\nIn my opinion it could limit future flexibility in case any other callers choose to implement such a function with different flags. Do let me know what you think.\n\nI have uploaded the patchset for this change already, but I am keeping this unresolved for any further discussion on weather callers may pass additional flags and if we should keep it as `bool scale` in the latest patchset or consider `FT_Int32 args`.",
      "parentUuid": "a4255739_e8bba4a2",
      "range": {
